# council-notify configuration (copy to ~/.council-notify.env, keep OUT of git).
# Fill ONE delivery method. Values are examples, not real.

# --- Option A: direct Telegram Bot API (reuses your existing bot) ---
# Bot token: from your Telegram bot setup (e.g. ~/.openclaw/telegram/bot-info-default.json
#   or from @BotFather). Chat id: your numeric id (ask @userinfobot) or a group id.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456789:AA...redacted...
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=987654321

# --- Option B: route through any command (e.g. your OpenClaw send hook / curl) ---
# {text}, {job_id}, {status} are substituted (shell-quoted).
# NOTIFY_CMD=curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:PORT/your-openclaw-send -d text={text}

# If neither is set, council-notify just prints to stdout (a local log).
